# UnrealMCP5_6_1 Codex Adapter

## Required Bootstrap

- Every new Codex session in this repository must read this file, then `codex/AGENTS.md`, then `codex/projects/UnrealMCP5_6_1.md`.
- After that minimal bootstrap, read only the role, policy, workflow, and component documents routed by the current request.
- Treat the embedded `codex/` tree as the repository-local operating authority after system, developer, runtime, and explicit user instructions.
- Ignore parent workspace instructions such as `D:\Git\AGENTS.md`. Do not require sibling repositories, Git submodules, or `../CubelessOps` for routine work in this checkout.
- `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP` is an ordinary tracked path in this repository, not an external submodule.
- The preferred local permission profile is defined in `codex/docs/policies/local-permission-profile.md`. If the active session is more restrictive, report that state before broad project or MCP work; this file cannot change runtime permissions.

## Repository And Worktree Safety

- Keep status, diffs, edits, staging, commits, pushes, and summaries scoped to this repository unless the user explicitly names another repository.
- Before substantial edits, inspect current status and recent history. Treat unfamiliar dirty or untracked files as another agent's in-flight work: do not edit, revert, stage, or commit them without explicit scope.
- Before pushing an existing tracked branch, pull with `--ff-only` and merge concurrently changed shared documents additively. Follow the Git policy for a new untracked branch.
- Follow `codex/docs/policies/git-repositories.md` for staging, remotes, repository boundaries, and push intent.
- Prefix agent-authored commit subjects with `[Codex]`, `[Claude]`, `[Codex+Claude]`, or `[Manual]` so authorship stays visible.

## Text Encoding Bootstrap

- Treat repository text as UTF-8 from the first read.
- In Windows PowerShell 5.1, always use `Get-Content -Encoding UTF8` for repository text and never rewrite a file from garbled terminal output.
- Preserve existing BOM and line-ending choices unless the current task explicitly changes them. Follow the complete rules in `codex/AGENTS.md`.

## Project Context

- Repository: `UnrealMCP5_6_1`; Cubeless integration/default branch: `main`.
- Primary engine target: Unreal Engine 5.6.1. Discover the effective engine root locally; the current project default is recorded in the project binding.
- UE 5.6.1 is an absolute capability boundary: new or ported MCP features must use APIs and editor behavior available in UE 5.6.1, and must not add UE 5.7/5.8-only functionality or future-engine compatibility branches.
- Resolve the effective configured editor bridge endpoint at runtime; its project default and override rules are recorded in the project binding.
- Keep Cubeless patches narrow and preserve UE 5.6.1 compatibility guards and stable fallback fields.

## Absolute Authoring Dependency Tripwire

- MCP and UnrealMCP are authoring tools only. Any generated or modified Blueprint, asset, level, material, Niagara system, PCG graph, component, helper API, or project content must continue to load, compile, cook, package, and run when the UnrealMCP plugin is disabled or absent, unless the user explicitly approves that exact dependency for the current task.
- Never persist `/Script/UnrealMCP`, `/UnrealMCP`, `UnrealMCP`, `MCPUnreal`, `mcp_unreal`, or another MCP-only class, function, component, module, graph, or object reference into finished project content by default.
- Apply this before mutation and before promotion or finalization. The canonical implementation and audit rules live in `codex/docs/policies/authoring-dependency-boundary.md`.

## Project C++ Absolute Approval Tripwire

- MCP agents must not create, modify, or promote project C++ by default. Prefer Blueprint, Widget Blueprint, Unreal Python, editor scripting, or MCP tool composition.
- Project C++ creation or modification is approved only when the user enters the current-task token as a standalone message `c++1218` or the explicit phrase `프로젝트 C++ 승인 c++1218`.
- General wording such as `승인`, `진행`, `해도 돼`, `수정해`, `좋아`, or `오케이` does not approve project C++.
- This gate covers `MCPGameProject/Source/**`, project runtime/editor modules, and non-MCP project-plugin C++ under `MCPGameProject/Plugins/*/Source/**`.
- C++ inside `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/**` is the sole standing path exception to the token. It may change conservatively for MCP tooling only when the MCP promotion gate is satisfied and finished results remain independent of UnrealMCP.
- Historical non-MCP plugin implementations or exceptions, including the existing `SkyDomeTools` VDB preview helper, do not approve future source edits. Future changes still require the current-task token.
- Follow `codex/docs/policies/project-cpp-approval-gate.md` before any source-like mutation, staging, or commit.

## Conditional Routing

- Use `codex/docs/workflows/component-reading-router.md` instead of reading every extension file.
- Do not automatically read PCG, AI texture, SkyDome, ControlRig, or another domain's documents during bootstrap. Read a component row only when the current request will actually inspect, edit, or verify that component.
- Selecting one component row never includes another row implicitly; combine rows only when the current task genuinely spans those components.
- For named roles, read the matching file under `codex/agents/`.
- For upstream synchronization, RPC/transport work, smoke tests, asset authoring, ControlRig, SkyDome, PCG, AI texture, packaging, or review, load only the workflow and component row that matches the request.
- For multi-asset or multi-step bridge work, consult `Docs/Tools/batch_tools.md` and coordinate any shared editor lifecycle action.

## Maintenance And Upstream

- Do not rewrite upstream files broadly. Keep the Cubeless patch small and reviewable.
- The approved command-handler split under `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Source/UnrealMCP/Private/Commands/` is limited to behavior-preserving separation with unchanged classes and routing.
- For requests such as `최신 업데이트`, `업데이트 받아줘`, `원본 pull`, `upstream 최신`, or `chongdashu 최신`, follow `codex/docs/workflows/mcp-upstream-update.md`.

## Verification Entry Point

- The canonical local dispatcher is `Python/scripts/analysis/run_verification.py`.
- Promotion that includes implementation, executable workflow/configuration, or shared contract changes requires the complete offline profile:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\run_verification.py --profile full
```

- During focused development, run the matching explicit profile: `core`, `catalog`, `transport`, `schema`, `niagara`, `write-observer`, `release-offline`, or `windows-transport`.
- Do not rerun `full` after every iterative edit. Use focused profiles during iteration and reserve `full` for a frozen checkpoint, final verification, release or `main` promotion, or an explicitly identified high-risk shared-core change.
- Pure instruction or documentation-only changes follow Tier 0 in `codex/docs/policies/cost-control.md` and do not trigger `full` solely because they will land on `main`; executable workflow or verification-manifest changes are not documentation-only.
- Focused profiles do not replace `full` when the complete offline profile is required. There is no automatic changed-file or path-based skip policy.
- Run live-editor smoke and UE builds only when the affected surface requires them, using the project binding and matching workflow. Avoid full source-engine rebuilds unless necessary or explicitly requested.
- GitHub Actions use the same dispatcher: the Ubuntu workflow calls `full`, and the Windows transport workflow calls `windows-transport`.
